{"title":"Ontario Mathematics Competition","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><p>The Ontario Mathematics Competition (OMC) is the annual contest of the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Ontario_Competitive_Mathematics_Committee\" title=\"Ontario Competitive Mathematics Committee\">Ontario Competitive Mathematics Committee</a>. \n</p><p>Designed as a student-ran counterpart to the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=CEMC_Pascal\" title=\"CEMC Pascal\">CEMC Pascal</a>, <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=CEMC_Cayley\" title=\"CEMC Cayley\">CEMC Cayley</a> and the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=CEMC_Fermat\" title=\"CEMC Fermat\">CEMC Fermat</a> contests and the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=AMC\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"AMC\">AMC</a>, the OMC consists of 25 multiple-choice questions to be completed in 60 minutes.\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Ontario_Mathematics_Competition_Problems_and_Solutions&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"Ontario Mathematics Competition Problems and Solutions (page does not exist)\">Ontario Mathematics Competition Problems and Solutions</a>\n</p><p><i>This article is a stub.  Help us out by <span class=\"plainlinks\"><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php?title=Ontario_Mathematics_Competition&amp;action=edit\">expanding it</a></span>.</i>\n</p>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261018102131\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU time usage: 0.009 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.016 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 7/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 334/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 0/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 4/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 0/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    5.652      1 Template:Stub\n100.00%    5.